WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.820 --> 00:00:06.820
A cuboid is simply a box like this.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:08.420
It is three-dimensional

00:00:08.660 --> 00:00:12.600
as it does not occupy a part of just one plane.

00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:15.120
Three things define a cuboid.

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:18.380
Length, its breadth and its height.

00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:20.680
This is a cuboid.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:23.260
What will be its surface area?

00:00:23.540 --> 00:00:25.020
As the name suggests,

00:00:25.140 --> 00:00:29.200
it will be the total area of all its surfaces.

00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:32.460
A cuboid has six surfaces in all.

00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:35.340
One at the front and one at the back.

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:37.560
Their areas will be equal

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:40.740
as it has a uniform cross section.

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:44.160
Area of each will be 'l times h'

00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:48.840
and the total area of both together will be '2lh'.

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:51.820
Similarly, the sum of the areas of the faces

00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:55.740
at the top and bottom together will be '2lb'.

00:00:55.940 --> 00:00:58.500
And the sum of the areas of the faces on the right

00:00:58.680 --> 00:01:02.020
and left will be '2bh'.

00:01:02.180 --> 00:01:05.400
That's the total surface area of a cuboid.

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:07.720
Taking the factor 2 common.

00:01:07.940 --> 00:01:13.840
We can write it as 'twice lh plus lb plus bh'.

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:16.840
What is its lateral surface area then?

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:20.100
The word lateral simply means side.

00:01:20.360 --> 00:01:23.840
This is the sum of the areas of the faces on the side.

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:26.940
Not the faces at the top or the bottom.

00:01:27.180 --> 00:01:31.700
So it will just be 'twice lh plus bh'.

00:01:31.940 --> 00:01:33.700
We ignored '2lb'

00:01:33.880 --> 00:01:37.800
as they are the areas of the top and bottom surfaces.

00:01:38.080 --> 00:01:40.520
So these are the two types of surface areas

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:43.020
we had to understand.

00:01:43.240 --> 00:01:46.580
The last concept is that of its volume.

00:01:46.820 --> 00:01:50.480
The volume of a cuboid is simply the product of its length,

00:01:50.720 --> 00:01:52.720
its breadth and its height.

00:01:53.060 --> 00:01:54.420
'lbh'

00:01:54.560 --> 00:02:00.520
To be more specific, it is the area of its base times its height.

00:02:00.740 --> 00:02:02.540
Knowing stuff about cuboids

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:05.660
also helps us understand its special case.

00:02:06.020 --> 00:02:08.020
The case of a cube.

00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:10.460
It looks similar to a cuboid.

00:02:10.600 --> 00:02:13.200
It has length, breadth and height

00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:17.600
with the only difference being that all three are equal.

00:02:17.920 --> 00:02:20.900
Let's say 'h' is equal to 's' units.

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:22.180
Think about it!

00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:24.360
If each of the sides are equal,

00:02:24.580 --> 00:02:27.160
then each face will be a square.

00:02:27.400 --> 00:02:30.840
The area of each face will be 's' squared.

00:02:31.060 --> 00:02:32.820
As there are six faces,

00:02:32.860 --> 00:02:37.180
the total surface area will be six 's' squared.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:41.220
What will be the lateral surface area and the volume then?

00:02:41.440 --> 00:02:43.700
As it has four faces on the side,

00:02:43.980 --> 00:02:47.880
its lateral surface area will be four 's' squared.

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:51.660
As 'l', 'b' and 'h' are all equal to 's',

00:02:51.960 --> 00:02:55.560
the volume of a cube will be side cubed.

00:02:55.780 --> 00:02:57.160
In the next session,

00:02:57.160 --> 00:03:02.900
we will look at the volume and surface area of a cylinder.

